A||||8||JohnnyK||Removing front cradle bolts...||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||09-21-2000||05:20 PM||||Well, I don't think the passenger side front cradle bolt will be a problem, but I cannot get the left one out. I got the nut out (Had to use the "special" impact gun my auto teacher calls Big Blue)... But the actual whole bolt will not turn. I tried using the gun on it for about 3 consecutive minutes, with no avail. I had someone use the gun while I nailed the other end of the bolt, to no avail... I put a johnson bar on it, and it seems I can turn it a bit, but it is stuck (and I mean really stuck) tot he rubber bushing. Seems like the same problem I had with the upper a-arm pivot bolts... Why is there a bushing in the cradle bolts anyways? With the a-arm, I had room to use an air chisel. I don't even have room to swing a ratchet in there (if I did, I wouldn't have these problems..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Any ideas. It should be soaking in penetrating oil at this moment.. Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||09-21-2000||05:27 PM||||Did you try a Ball joint fork? If it will fit/work. Just a thought||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||09-21-2000||06:32 PM||||I've had a few like that! Resorted to using a body jack on it to press the thing out. If you don't have access to one the fastest way to do it is to buy a new bushing for it and use a heat wrench to get the cradle loose.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-21-2000||07:06 PM||||look back thru the last weeks postings for my note about installing polly bushings. I think the topic is "pollyurethane install".||||reg||1
Z||000004||rprevo||09-22-2000||12:53 AM|||| My Passenger front bolt was rusted into the bushing and I eneded up useing a die grinder<BR>with a cut off wheel, I cut the bolt between<BR>the frame and the bushing and slipped the<BR>cradle down and replaced the bushing.<BR>Good luck,<P> Ray<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000005||JohnnyK||09-22-2000||03:49 PM||||I tried everything... Had to finally use acetylene and melt it, and it still just barely turns. I think on monday I can use the impact socket on front of the bolt, and hammer on the back and get it off.. Anyoen got a bushing they don't need?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||09-22-2000||04:36 PM||||If you melted the bushing when you try to get it out on Monday, heat it back up so when you smack it it will come loose off the sleeve inside. WATCH YOU TOES! And double check your support, don't want it to fall!||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||09-22-2000||05:10 PM||||Trust me, it won't be that easy... I heated it today and started waking it and impacting it. Still wouldn't budge.. But by then I was getting pretty weak...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||09-23-2000||10:55 PM||||Sounds like you'll just have to melt the head off it and the threads to just inside the bracket. Watch the splash metal.||||reg||1
